//@version=6
indicator("UCTPROBE_EXCHANGE", overlay = false)

// ⭐⭐ THE KEYED FIELD. `symbolScope.json::confirmed` is keyed on OUR store's
// exchange string and its value is the string TRADINGVIEW's `syminfo.exchange`
// returns. This probe reads THAT field, and nothing else settles it.
//
// ⚰️ WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL — the five-symbol capture of 2026-09-09
// (`tests/fixtures/vendor/barstate-realtime-spy-2026-09-09.json` ::
// `tickerid_shape_five_symbols`) read `syminfo.ticker` and `syminfo.tickerid`.
// Both are real measurements and both are still correct FOR THEIR OWN QUESTION
// (Volume line 222's slash containment, `tickerid-containment.pine`). Neither is
// the field the map is keyed on, so `confirmed` could not be filled from them —
// doing so would be the "assertion wearing a data structure" symbolScope.json
// warns against. ⛔ THE TWO PROBES ARE NOT INTERCHANGEABLE. That is the whole
// reason this is a separate file rather than an edit to that one.
//
// ⛔⛔ AND THE CAPTURE PROVED THEY CAN DISAGREE. `SP:SPX` was requested and the
// vendor resolved it to `SP_DLY:SPX` — so the tickerid prefix is not even the
// text the member typed, let alone guaranteed to equal `syminfo.exchange`.
// N11 below measures that gap directly instead of assuming it away.

// ── the instrument ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ⭐ EQUALITY, NOT CONTAINMENT, AND THAT IS THE POINT. A member's script writes
// `syminfo.exchange == "AMEX"`, Pine compares strings with `==`, so the probe
// asks the question in the member's own operator. Containment would answer a
// DIFFERENT and weaker question: `str.contains("NASDAQ", "SP")` is false but
// `str.contains("SP_DLY", "SP")` is true, which is exactly how a whitelist built
// on containment "looks correct on this one example" while being wrong.
//
// ⚠️ THE CANDIDATE SET IS A WHITELIST OF WHAT WE EXPECT, NOT AN ENUMERATION OF
// WHAT THE VENDOR CAN EMIT. It is `store_to_pine`'s distinct values. A symbol
// whose exchange is none of these reads 0 on every line below — which is an
// ANSWER (see N10), not a gap, and it must be recorded as unconfirmed rather
// than rounded to the nearest 1.
plot(syminfo.exchange == "AMEX"   ? 1 : 0, "eq_AMEX")     // N1
plot(syminfo.exchange == "NASDAQ" ? 1 : 0, "eq_NASDAQ")   // N2
plot(syminfo.exchange == "NYSE"   ? 1 : 0, "eq_NYSE")     // N3
plot(syminfo.exchange == "CBOE"   ? 1 : 0, "eq_CBOE")     // N4
plot(syminfo.exchange == "OTC"    ? 1 : 0, "eq_OTC")      // N5

// The five feeds the prior capture already visited, so the two runs can be laid
// side by side on the same symbols rather than compared across different ones.
plot(syminfo.exchange == "FX"       ? 1 : 0, "eq_FX")       // N6
plot(syminfo.exchange == "BITSTAMP" ? 1 : 0, "eq_BITSTAMP") // N7
plot(syminfo.exchange == "SP"       ? 1 : 0, "eq_SP")       // N8
plot(syminfo.exchange == "SP_DLY"   ? 1 : 0, "eq_SP_DLY")   // N9

// ⭐⭐ N10 IS WHAT MAKES A ZERO ROW READABLE. If every equality above is 0 the
// length still names how long the real answer is, so an unmeasured spelling
// arrives as "6 characters, none of my candidates" instead of "none of the
// above" — the difference between a lead and a shrug.
plot(str.length(syminfo.exchange), "len_exchange")        // N10

// ⭐⭐ N11 IS THE CROSS-FIELD QUESTION, and it is the one that retires the idea
// that the old capture could have been reused. 1 = `syminfo.exchange` appears
// inside `syminfo.tickerid`; 0 = the two fields disagree outright. On SP:SPX the
// prior capture already showed the tickerid prefix is `SP_DLY`, so this line is
// where "is the prefix the exchange?" stops being a guess.
plot(str.contains(syminfo.tickerid, syminfo.exchange) ? 1 : 0, "exch_in_tickerid") // N11

// ⛔ N12 IS THE NON-VACUITY CONTROL AND IT IS NOT OPTIONAL. Every plot above can
// legitimately read 0. Without a channel that is known-nonzero on every symbol,
// "this symbol matched nothing" and "the study never evaluated" are the SAME ROW
// of zeros, and a capture that cannot tell those apart is not evidence.
// `syminfo.ticker` is served today and is never empty, so a 0 here means the
// probe is broken and the whole row must be discarded.
plot(str.length(syminfo.ticker), "len_ticker_CONTROL")    // N12

// ── how to run it ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ⛔ FOLLOW `docs/pine/capture-procedure.md`. In particular: never add a study
// while the tab is hidden (`insertStudy` returns cleanly and inserts NOTHING —
// verify by re-reading `model().dataSources()`, never by the absence of a
// throw), and restore symbol, resolution, pane stretch factors and study
// visibility afterwards. The browser is shared with other sessions.
//
// ⭐ THIS IS A VALUE CAPTURE, so it is immune to the hidden-tab RENDERING defect
// once the study is on the chart: read `study._data._items`, which is populated
// whether or not a pixel was ever drawn. Adding the study still needs a visible
// tab.
//
// WITNESSES — one per DISTINCT STORE SPELLING, because the map is per-exchange
// and not per-symbol. The bounded half of the store vocabulary is `_YF_EXCHANGE`
// in `api/services/ticker_meta.py`, measured at SIX distinct values:
//
//     store spelling   suggested witness   what it settles
//     'NYSE Arca'      SPY                 the flagship divergence: our store
//                                          says 'NYSE Arca' and the 2026-09-09
//                                          capture already showed the tickerid
//                                          prefix is AMEX
//     'NASDAQ'         AAPL
//     'NYSE'           JPM
//     'NYSE American'  an NYSE-American-listed name
//     'Cboe BZX'       a Cboe-BZX-listed ETF
//     'OTC'            an OTC name
//
// ⛔⛔ SIX, NOT FIVE. A five-symbol run cannot cover six spellings, so a repeat
// of the previous run's symbol count leaves at least one store spelling
// unwitnessed and its `confirmed` entry unfillable. Record every symbol you
// actually visit, including the ones that matched nothing.
//
// ⚠️ AND SIX IS ONLY THE BOUNDED HALF. `_YF_EXCHANGE` is a closed set; the FMP
// leg (`row.get('exchange') or row.get('exchangeShortName')`) is free vendor
// text and cannot be enumerated from here, which is why `store_to_pine` carries
// spellings — 'NASDAQ Global Select', 'New York Stock Exchange' — that no
// `_YF_EXCHANGE` value produces. Those need their own witnesses or they stay
// unconfirmed, and a symbol carrying an unnamed spelling REFUSES rather than
// guessing. That is the intended failure direction, not a gap to close by
// filling in the blanks.
//
// RECORDING — every `confirmed` entry needs all four of `{pine, witness,
// captured, how}`. An entry without a witness is an assertion wearing a data
// structure. Name the invocation in the result JSON the way
// `tools/record_clock_parity.py` names its own, so the next reader can
// reproduce the row rather than trust it:
//
//     "_invocation": "tools/visual_conformance/probes/exchange-spelling.pine
//                     pasted into the TradingView editor; plot values read from
//                     study._data._items per docs/pine/capture-procedure.md"
